+
+## Security policy and release checks
+
+The build finaliser hashes the exact inline scripts in every generated HTML
+page, including noindex and error pages, and writes those hashes to
+`dist/.htaccess`. Unapproved inline JavaScript, event-handler attributes and
+`eval` are blocked. Base URLs and embedded objects are disabled; form actions
+and framing are restricted to the same origin. Existing inline styles remain
+allowed to preserve presentation. Production permits the pinned analytics
+script and its origin for connections; review builds omit those exceptions.
+
+`npm run verify` runs source validation, 51 isolated PHP checks, security-policy
+regressions, Astro checks/build and generated-output validation. The latter
+requires the exact policy for the generated scripts and checks the analytics
+attributes and build mode. `npm run release:package` repeats these checks in
+production mode before freezing the release. Deploy generated HTML and its
+`.htaccess` together; do not edit HTML or script hashes after packaging.
+
+For browser checks using the enforced generated CSP, run `npm run build` then
+`node tests/forms/serve-ui.mjs`. Open `http://127.0.0.1:4340/__qa/csp` for the
+blocking probe and `/contact/` or `/events/` for mocked form interactions.
+The fixture refuses production builds, sends no email and uses synthetic
+scenario addresses documented in its source. Astro preview alone does not
+enforce Apache headers.
+
+The November security changes are local pending an explicitly authorised
+production deployment and live header/resource checks. Building a release is
+not deployment approval.
